From 79c0c0db71ada65cdf7dd6792fab60d494fda183 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christoph Keller <christoph.keller@gmx.net>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:00:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xrdp-accel-assist: destroy encoders before exit to avoid
 NVENC hang

When the RDP client disconnects, xrdp-accel-assist detects EOF on the xrdp
transport, logs "exit" and returns from main() with its NVENC encoder
sessions still open. exit() then runs an exit handler of NVIDIA's
libnvcuvid.so.1 (loaded via libnvidia-encode) which joins a worker thread
that is blocked on a mutex inside libnvcuvid, so the process never
terminates (Linux, NVIDIA driver 595.84, RTX 3090 Ti, Ubuntu 24.04,
glibc 2.39).

The helper proxies the xorgxrdp <-> xrdp connection, so Xorg never sees
EOF on its socketpair, rdpClientConDisconnect() never runs, and every
disconnected session keeps an NVENC session and ~300 MiB of VRAM until
the next reconnect or the end of the session.

Destroying the encoders first (xrdp_accel_assist_x11_delete_all_pixmaps(),
the existing teardown: nvEncDestroyEncoder etc.) avoids the deadlock; the
process then exits normally. The early error returns in main() happen
before any encoder exists and are not affected.

Backtrace of the hung helper (all threads, symbols from libc/libcuda/
libnvcuvid only): thread 1 exit() -> libnvcuvid exit handler -> thread
join; worker thread pthread_mutex_lock() in libnvcuvid.

Reproduce: Xorg session with the NVIDIA driver (xorg_nvidia.conf),
XRDP_USE_ACCEL_ASSIST=1, connect with a GFX/H.264 client (FreeRDP 3.32
/gfx:AVC444), disconnect: before this change the helper stays alive and
nvidia-smi keeps listing it (3 of 3 attempts).
Verified: 3 connect/disconnect cycles, helper exits within 10 s each
time, encoder session count back to 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VLJpmVyG6ghcutrcFH3F8v
---
 xrdp_accel_assist/xrdp_accel_assist.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xrdp_accel_assist/xrdp_accel_assist.c b/xrdp_accel_assist/xrdp_accel_assist.c
index 03709592..2edc3ba1 100644
--- a/xrdp_accel_assist/xrdp_accel_assist.c
+++ b/xrdp_accel_assist/xrdp_accel_assist.c
@@ -1027,5 +1027,8 @@ main(int argc, char **argv)
         }
     }
     LOG(LOG_LEVEL_INFO, "exit");
+    /* destroy the encoder sessions before exit(): with live NVENC sessions
+     * an exit handler in NVIDIA's libnvcuvid can deadlock (Linux driver) */
+    xrdp_accel_assist_x11_delete_all_pixmaps();
     return 0;
 }
